[I] Call audio routing daemon

[T] callaudiod is a daemon for dealing with audio routing during phone calls
[T] on mobile Linux devices. It provides a D-Bus interface allowing other
[T] programs to switch audio profiles, route output to the speaker or back
[T] to its original port, and mute the microphone.

[U] https://gitlab.com/mobian1/callaudiod/

[A] droidian
